the outcome [1]. Recent work in clinical decision analysis has focused on the
\par
establishment of \&dquo;natural\&dquo; utility systems for medical problems; many cur-
\par
rent applications of clinical decision analysis utilize quality-adjusted life
\par
expectancies as relevant outcome measures [2,3].
\par
The decision-analytic formalism works well for problems involving
\par
