\par
transitions: P WW' Pwig P wd, Pm P,d, Pdd{$\cdot$} These probabilities are abstracted
\par
from the clinical literature, or may represent experts' assessments. In the
\par
clinical literature, state transitions are commonly expressed as rates. Rates
\par
can range from zero to infinity and are expressed per unit time (e.g., \&dquo;The
\par
mortality rate with disease X is two percent per year. \&dquo;). Probabilities, on the
\par
other hand, vary from zero to one and have time built into them implicitly.
