\par
take advantage of the state model, however, and assign different quality-of-
\par
life measurements to each clinical classification. This differential assign-
\par
ment introduces the concept of incremental utility. In standard decision
\par
theory, the utility associated with a given length of survival is represented by
\par
a function of time. In the Markov formulation, we assess a state-dependent431
