\par
The Markov model can keep track of incremental utility in two ways. If
\par
quality adjustments are the only utility factor of interest, then the expected
\par
time a patient spends in each state of the Markov process may be multiplied
\par
by its corresponding fractional utility; these adjusted survivals are then
\par
added to yield quality-adjusted life expectancy. If time-dependent adjust-
\par
