\par
ined systematically using techniques of sensitivity analysis. Of greatest
\par
interest is the etiology of the presenting cerebral hemorrhage. Because of its
\par
intrinsic interest we kept this chance event in the decision tree proper, out-
\par
side of the Markov utility structure, to facilitate sensitivity analysis. We
\par
varied the likelihood of primary cerebral hemorrhage over the range from
\par
0.8 to 0.95, corresponding to the range suggested by the panel of radiolo-
\par
gists. At all values over this interval the preferred decision is to withhold
\par
anticoagulation. Figure 11 expands this sensitivity analysis to all conceivable
\par
