\par
utility values from the cohort analysis (45 percent in the Markov chain for-
\par
mulation).
\par
Within the Markov model of prognosis, several variables may be exam-
\par
ined. The embolic rate, 184 events/1000 patient-years without anticoagula-
\par
tion, was taken as a maximum value. Any lesser value further favors with-
\par
holding anticoagulation at this time. Similarly, the values pertaining to the
\par
risks of anticoagulation were taken at their minima. Any increase in these
\par
would favor withholding anticoagulation.446
