\par
decision analysis useful as a predictive tool but of less value as a
\par
prescriptive tool.
\par
We observed that decision makers often agree with the logic of decision
\par
analysis but feel uncomfortable at an intuitive level with its implications.
\par
Far from encouraging departure from traditional economic analysis, this
\par
paper may satisfy decision makers that what is currently omitted from
\par
expected utility analysis deserves to be omitted and that a formal analysis
\par
may be exactly what is needed to prevent a decision maker's intuition
\par
from forcing economically inefficient decisions.
