\par
financial return in order to avoid regret will exhibit some of the behavioral
\par
paradoxes of decision theory. By explicitly incorporating regret, expected
\par
utility theory not only becomes a better descriptive predictor but also may
\par
become a more convincing guide for prescribing behavior to decision makers.
