1. INCORPORATING REGRET INTO A UTILITY FUNCTION
\par
The concept of multiattribute utility theory is well established through
\par
considerable theoretical development and by numerous applications
\par
(Keeney and Raiffa [1976]). For those decision makers who do experience
\par
regret and are prepared to make tradeoffs to reduce it, including regret
\par
explicitly in an analysis makes sense. We will assume that appropriate
\par
