The December editorial in \textbf{\emph{The Chartered Accountant in Australia }}revealed a
\par
change of mood. `Gigantic company losses disclosed in recent months have, under-
\par
standably, shaken the confidence of a wide section of the Australian public' (p.
\par
\textbf{32 1 }) . It was not suggested that such suddenly-revealed losses posed problems for
\par
the profession; rather they `evoked the oft-repeated call' for a `watchdog on public
\par
