In the Victorian parliament, it was claimed that the Institute `had not been
\par
jealous enough of the reputation of its members'; the absence of professional self-
\par
regulation meant that `some time, some Government would legislate ``to register
\par
stockbrokers, accountants, and all'' ' \textbf{\emph{(The Bulletin, 14 }}December \textbf{1963).}
