\par
and work-in-progress for the previous year had been overstated by \textbf{\$2.4 }million,
\par
and the auditors considered this to be a trading loss, which should reduce profit
\par
for \textbf{1968 }or \textbf{1969, }or both. Directors agreed that the assets should be reduced
\par
to the `correct' figure, but did not consider that the item should be offset against
\par
trading, and advised that they had received `the advice of senior counsel' that their
