\par
In one sense, a decade of work in the area of individual
\par
rights in our industrial society came to fruition that afternoon
\par
in Birmingham. By that, I do not imply that any "single-
\par
handed" effort achieved the present complex processes of the
\par
EEOC. At least a dozen, perhaps twenty people were, in the
\par
