\par
in negotiation, and his dedication to the preservation of indi-
\par
vidual rights to combat employment discrimination, made us
\par
an effective working team then and afterwards when he
\par
served as Acting Director of Compliance and Acting General
\par
Counsel for EEOC.
\par
The work of conciliations that first year was done largely
\par
by Holbert, myself and four other men who contributed in
