\textbf{The model}
\par
The Change Model offers an extension to the commander model by addressing the question
\par
\textbf{`I }have a strategy-now how do I get my organization to implement it?' In this model, the
\par
CEO applies behavioural science techniques to manipulate his organization into compliance
\par
with his strategic plan. The role of the CEO is that of an architect, designing administrative
\par
systems to orchestrate implementation and push his inertia-ridden economic unit toward
\par
goal achievement.
\par
This approach starts where the Commander Model ends: with implementation. It
\par
assumes that the economic tools described above for strategy formulation have been
