\par
American managers seeking the panacea to their recent economic woes in the face of
\par
successful Japanese competition.
\par
To a large extent, proponents of the Cultural Model have modernized some of the human
\par
relations approaches of the 1950s (see, for example, Likert, 1961), or the `human resources'
\par
