\par
(Ouchi and Price, 1978), and `super-ordinate goals' and `style' (Waterman \emph{et al., }1980); \emph{(2)}
\par
these writers focus on the entire organization-a significantly larger unit of analysis than
\par
the face-to-face work group of the human relations era; and \textbf{(3) }they argue that corporate
\par
culture should serve as the handmaiden to corporate strategy, rather than to proselytize
\par
`power equalization' and the like for its own sake.
