\par
when they anticipated non-conformity with top management goals-often without the goals
\par
being explicitly articulated. In other words, goals were inferred (at lower levels), or the
\par
perceptions of goals were shaped, by the signals inherent in previous judgements (decisions)
\par
made by the CEO.
