\par
one. An extension might be:
\par
Pt = St + x (Pt, - St)
\par
where x is a decision rule coefficient to be specified between zero and one, and
\par
Pt-, represents production in the previous time period. If x = 1, then the sales
\par
terms cancel out, and production in this period equals production in the previous
\par
