\par
to say.62 Even so, the potentially problematical diminution of preferred
\par
shareholder participation in corporate governance stems not from the
\par
fact that participation is almost totally a matter of contract, but from the
\par
courts' occasionally dubious approach to contract interpretation, espe-
\par
cially in the shadow of the partial but incomplete regulation of some par-
\par
ticipation rights by statute.
\par
\emph{a. The Example of a New Issuance}
\par
A related problem is the issuance of new preferred stock that can
\par
affect current shareholders' interests. Typically the shareholders have no
\par
decisionmaking power as to the issuance of specific preferred stock.63
\par
This is not inevitable but rather arises from the historical invention and
\par
judicial acceptance of the concept of issuing preferred stock in separate
\par
series within a single umbrella class.6 The shareholders authorize the
\par
class in the articles of incorporation by a pro forma, boilerplate enabling
\par
provision. It is authorized completely without attributes, as a "blank
\par
stock"-today a term of art.65
\par
The justification for this approach was originally and remains the
\par
instrumental need for flexibility. Such stock, limited in its financial re-
\par
turns to a set or at least a capped amount, must compete in financial
\par
markets. Thus, it must be priced with exogenous as well as firm-endoge-
\par
nous factors in mind. It cannot simply be issued at a price determined by
\par
a preordained relation to the going prices for the firm's residual stock.66
\par
Because of practical constraints, this flexibility is inconsistent with a re-
\par
quirement for shareholder approval of stock issuance in all but the small-
\par
est corporation. Director approval heretofore was considered
\par
appropriate for specific issuance in series form. The only shareholders
\par
who do participate in stock issuance are the holders of previously issued
\par
preferred shares, and then usually only if those shares are materially af-
