\par
hostile merger proposal.'1 0 This is both one of the less appealing and,
\par
luckily, less effective weapons in the shark repellent arsenal of target
\par
companies. It effects a shift in voting power which undermines the level
\par
of shareholder participation in corporate governance that is essential to
\par
corporation law. This is true whether participation is viewed from an
\par
economic efficiency or constitutionalist perspective.
\par
Shareholder participation is important in the economic model,
\par
which postulates a takeover market for control of the corporation, in-
\par
