One objection derives from traditional antitrust policy. Information
\par
differs only in degree from a variety of otherwise analogous investments
\par
like research and development, advertising that generates goodwill, mar-
\par
ket development costs, and similar expenditures or "properties." Never-
\par
theless, challenges to freeriding rivals-who pirate dress designs, infringe
\par
