\par
There are several points here. The first is that the acquisition of knowl-
\par
edge is dependent on interaction and is done while the individual is moving
\par
through the performance of various tasks. The second is that the acquired
\par
knowledge can affect the individual's task performance on future tasks. The
\par
final point is that this article is not about task performance; hence, no model
\par
