\par
part of the social knowledge base, the first, were it to become accepted by
\par
the members of the social unit and so become a part of the social knowledge
\par
base, it would be only a minor modification in current shared knowledge,
\par
whereas the second would require more extensive modification of social
\par
knowledge. Note, that both concepts 1 and 2 are part of the social knowledge
\par
base but neither concept 4 nor concept 5 are part of this base. Hence, for the
\par
fact 1 - - 2 to become part of the social knowledge base no education
\par
would be required. It just needs to be communicated enough. Further, since
\par
there are several facts in the social knowledge base that already utilize the430
