Other sources of information will depend on
\par
the specific institutional environment of the
\par
employee representative. Union branch meetings
\par
and joint Shop Stewards Committees serve as
\par
channels for the communication of local informa-
\par
tion on pay and conditions. The pamphlets
\par
produced by the Labour Research Department,
\par
the Institute of Workers' Control, Social Audit and
\par
Counter-Information Services, provide information
\par
obtained from a variety of sources (of varying
\par
reliability) about the economic and social
\par
performance of specific companies. Finally the
\par
Trades Union Research Unit, Ruskin College,
\par
Oxford, has produced fully documented pay
\par
claims for use in negotiations. For example, the
\par
Ford Wage Claim (T.G.W.U. 1971a) and the I.C.I.
\par
Claim (T.G.W.U. 1971b) used a variety of sources
\par
to substantiate their claims to find out about the
\par
companies.
