\par
This study is presented in three related papers. The first develops a structure
\par
for making decisions regarding Caltrans/PATH research. It describes a
\par
research cycle in which real world needs and opportunities fed into a process
\par
by which research priorities are set, proposals invited, and projects are
\par
selected. These research projects ultimately provide information that can be
\par
used for further research or for implementation. Implementation changes
\par
