\textbf{I }Disputes about styles of construction cut across all provisions, and many branches of
\par
constitutional law seem to have common roots. For a demonstration that the tests under most
\par
of the principal sources of limitations on governmental power turn out to be identical, see
\par
Sunstein, \emph{Naked Preferences and the Constitution, }84 CoLum. L. REv. (forthcoming Nov. 1984).\textbf{19841}
\par
