\par
a mixture of objectives. Congress has many members, each with a
\par
separate purpose or meaning. Part of the process of compromise may
\par
be to put a few general-interest and a few private-interest provisions
\par
in one bill.
\par
One way to approach the problem is to ask whether the statute is
\par
specific or general. The more detailed the law, the more evidence of
\par
