\par
sess. General-interest statutes, on the other hand, are designed to
\par
vest discretion in courts, to transfer the locus of decision; courts
\par
implementing general statutes (such as the antitrust laws) become the
\par
decisionmakers. The decisions of courts are the things for which the
\par
parties bargained, and so judicial power to extemporize is at its great-
\par
est.
