\emph{C. Other Applications of Ex Ante Analysis}
\par
I have examined the Court's treatment of intellectual property to
\par
bring out the Court's shifting emphasis toward ex ante analysis, but
\par
almost any other subject would have done as well. Tort cases often
\par
invite the Court to divide the stakes (or dip into a "deep pocket")
\par
without careful attention to the effects of its rules on future behavior.
\par
For example, in the 1953 Term the Court abolished the doctrine of
\par
contributory negligence in admiralty by calling it "harsh" and by
\par
