\emph{C. Interest Groups, State Laws,}
\par
\emph{and the Preservation of Competition}
\par
A recognition of the interest-group nature of much legislation does
\par
not necessarily lead courts to become the passive agents of the pre-
\par
vailing factions. Quite the contrary, when the factions prevail in the
\par
