and overlapping laws and policies. The task of this Court, therefore, is to interpret the
\par
statutory language that Congress enacted into law. Careful attention to the statutory
\par
language is especially important in an area as technical and complex as banking law,
\par
where the policies actually enacted into law are complicated and difficult for a nonspe-
\par
-cialist judiciary to discern in their proper perspective.
