\par
restrictions on borrowing or spot sales the price of security could be calculated
\par
by first calculating the certainty equivalent of its return and then dividing that
\par
by the safe rate of interest. The certainty equivalent return was the mean return
\par
minus the "cost of risk"---a risk discount factor times the covariance of the security
\par
with the market as a whole.
