\par
be shown that the value of the firm will depend on the financial policy of the firm.
\par
At the present time the general equilibrium theory under uncertainty is in a rather
\par
unsatisfactory state. It is not even clear what are the empirical phenomena which
\par
the model should explain. For instance, although many economists would argue that
\par
it is obvious that firms face downward sloping demand curves for their shares and
\par
that their market value depends on their debt equity ratio, others might well
\par
