\par
The experience with private arbitration really doesn't tell us anything at all
\par
about what kinds of procedural rules are most favored. The reason is that
\par
people who have chosen to arbitrate have selected themselves as people who
\par
have enough mutual interest to work out their own problems. That is a very
\par
desirable frame of mind for people to be in. It's too bad most litigants are not
\par
of such a mind. But they are not and so compulsory litigation results.
