when the initial starting point also favors the dominant party.
\par
The next part of our analysis covers contractual relationships between the
\par
parties or when the parties have the option to contract around the legal rule
\par
and to use the market. That is summed up in Figure 2 where we define the
\par
cost of using the market and have a truncated or discontinuous curve indi-
\par
cating that in some regions it pays for the parties to use the market because
