\par
contingencies of the outer environment. To live effectively is to live with
\par
adequate information. It is possible to interpret the information carried by a
\par
message as essentially the negative of its entropy. That is, the more probable
\par
the message, the less information it gives.'2 Among the many ideals we have
\par
for our meanings, one of the most important is that our meanings \textbf{be }as sharp
\par
as possible. But it is surprising how many of the puzzling questions occur
\par
in a context of talking about talking, where we have a system dealing with
\par
itself. In psychology certainly, theory and meta-theory are often confused.
