\par
This Lincolnesque idea that "the people
\par
can't be fooled" may be based upon view-
\par
ing the underlying world process as sto-
\par
chastically stationary, so that individuals
\par
can gradually learn both about the effects
\par
of events upon prices and about the proba-
\par
bility distribution of events. However, this
\par
