\par
\textbf{place on release and/or utilization of information. These effects are purely redistributive; that is, they}
\par
\textbf{may not add much social value. However, for private firms they may be attractive insofar as they lead}
\par
\textbf{to the appreciation of assets }or \textbf{stocks for one firm at the expense of other firms. Hirshleifer 11 1 , p.}
\par
\textbf{5711 argued that if Eli Whitney (who invented the cotton gin) had speculated on the implications of}
\par
\textbf{his invention for the price of cotton and cotton-bearing land, he might have realized benefits far ex-}
\par
\textbf{ceeding the value of his patent on the gin. For a few counterarguments, see [16, footnote 21.}
