\par
discrimination rationale. Both the utility of the appraisal right to share-
\par
holders and the optimal valuation objective may also depend on the type
\par
of fundamental change and corporation type. The \textbf{\emph{CBCA }}and cognate
\par
statutes do not currently make these distinctions.
\par
The practical problems of designing and administering an effective
\par
appraisal right are considered in Part V; these include the allocation of
\par
the burden of costs, taxation of the award, questions of procedure, and
\par
other issues relating to the workability of the current statutory appraisal
\par
right. It would appear that the current provisions are inadequate in a
\par
number of important respects. Suggestions are made for improvements.
