\par
change may be consummated if it causes the market price of the firm's securities to drop. This
\par
would protect shareholders against fundamental changes that decrease security values. However,
\par
there are practical problems that would attend such a provision, including the determination of
\par
whether or not the company's securities diminished in value as a \emph{consequence }of the proposed
\par
change. Only sophisticated regression techniques will yield an answer to this question. Courts, as a
\par
practical matter, would be substantially unable to review this factual question without resort to\textbf{\emph{CANADA-UNITED STATES LAW JOURNAL}}
