missible discrimination results primarily from the tension between the
\par
facilitation of the economic gains which may arise from permitting sub-
\par
stantively unequal treatment on fundamental changes, and the dangers of
\par
opportunistic redistribution (and the associated economic losses) engen-
\par
dered by such a rule. Thus, the discussion in this section will focus on
