stances. It will be suggested that the value of the appraisal right to share-
\par
holders and the optimal form of valuation objective will depend on the
\par
relative danger of opportunistic redistribution associated with different
\par
types of fundamental changes and the degree to which the appraisal right
\par
(and the associated valuation principle) is likely to reduce the frequency
\par
of productive fundamental changes.\emph{CANADA-UNITED STATES LAW }\textbf{\emph{JOURNAL}}
