1. Pure going-private transactions
\par
a) \emph{Pure going-private transaction defined}
\par
\textbf{A }"going-private transaction" is one that forcibly evicts participat-
\par
ing shareholders from the enterprise so as to concentrate corporate con-
\par
trol and the residual interest in earnings and assets in the hands of a
\par
single shareholder or small group of shareholders. A "pure" going-pri-
\par
vate transaction is a going-private transaction effected by insider manag-
\par
