\par
b) \emph{A role for the appraisal right}
\par
At least in theory, it would appear that there exists significant dan-
\par
ger of opportunism associated with pure going-private transactions. As
\par
noted earlier, an invitation to opportunism arises from the asymmetric
\par
possession of information by insider majority (or controlling) sharehold-
\par
