\par
likelihood of real economic gains. But, as with pure going-private trans-
\par
actions, there are dangers associated with the exploitation of inside infor-
\par
mation. These transactions present the same post-transaction
\par
monitoring problem as pure going-private transactions do. Thus, the rel-
\par
ative worth of a valuation principle yielding participation in hidden val-
\par
ues (or full transaction synergies, discussed below) increases where the
\par
parent is a private rather than public corporation.
