\par
given the heterogeneity of interests to be protected in a private corpora-
\par
tion and the relatively large variance in the type of financial contract
\par
struck, mandatory rules will unduly inhibit the process of contracting to
\par
achieve the accommodation of specific preferences. It would appear that
\par
presumptive rather than mandatory rules are indicated.
\par
The dominant form of corporate enterprise in Canada is the public
\par
company whose shares trade in thin markets. Such companies appear at
\par
