\textbf{212 }This might be so for a number of reasons: where, for example, the degree of opportunistic
\par
behaviour engaged in by shareholding majorities is not great, where other legal remedies (or the
\par
market) are an adequate answer to problems of opportunism, where the costs of the appraisal right
\par
(to shareholders and to the company) overwhelm any gains which arise, or where there is some
\par
combination of these or other factors.\textbf{\emph{CANADA-UNITED STATES LAW JOURNAL}}
