\emph{overcompensation }of appraisal claimants even where a broader valuation
\par
objective is indicated, resulting in excessive use of the appraisal right and
\par
a corresponding discouragement of fundamental changes. It is better to
\par
improve both the theoretical and practical accuracy of the accounting
\par
process by clarifying the valuation objective and fashioning procedures
\par
that are designed to make achievement of that objective possible.
