\emph{D. Private Companies}
\par
Private companies present the greatest conceptual and practical dif-
\par
ficulties for the valuation of minority shareholdings. Many small, private
\par
corporations are essentially incorporated partnerships; shareholders are
\par
often actively involved in the management of the corporation, and the
\par
