\emph{E. Valuation Date}
\par
As noted above, the \emph{CBCA }and cognate statutes instruct the court to
\par
fix fair value at the close of business on the day before the resolution
\par
approving the fundamental change is adopted.24 It would be more ap-
\par
propriate to fix the valuation date at the time when the shareholder, hav-
\par
ing claimed the right, loses rights as a shareholder and is entitled only to
\par
a payment of interest on the appraised value of the shares. Since this
\par
date might vary for shareholders claiming the right,242 convenience sug-
\par
gests that a valuation date be fixed at the end of the period during which
\par
they lose their rights as shareholders. 24
