Moreover, the risks of opportunism associated with such events (at least,
\par
as between managers and shareholders or shareholders \emph{inter se) }are likely
\par
to be far less than in significant structural or constitutional changes, and
\par
in most cases there will be no such risk at all. Thus, the statutory selec-
