\emph{A. Aspirational Approaches to Negotiation Ethics}
\par
With growing use of negotiation, aspirational ethics are particularly
\par
important as guides toward higher ethical standards. However, ap-
\par
proaches that might be useful in negotiation place too little emphasis on
\par
the unique operational characteristics of the negotiation process. These
\par
process characteristics are necessary for an eventual understanding of the
\par
appropriate use of aspirational ethics in the specialized bargaining
\par
process.
\par
The four approaches discussed here are drawn largely from legal
\par
contexts67 because ethics are best understood not abstractly, but within a
\par
