Universalism does not help in distinguishing among these dilemmas.
\par
For example, Rubin argues for a duty of candor, including voluntary
\par
disclosure during negotiations, because "[h]onesty implies not only tell-
\par
ing [the] literal truth but also disclosing the whole truth."' 0 What, then,
\par
is the point of the strategic dealings that are the modus operandi of the
\par
