\emph{B. A Functionalist Model for Negotiation Ethics}
\par
Functionalism is a model that provides a way to analyze and test the
\par
ethics of the bargaining process as it operates through the bargaining
\par
techniques used by negotiators. Functionalism therefore differs from
\par
static models that are self-contained systems. For example, functional-
\par
ism differs from aspirational approaches in its goals and in its focus. Its
\par
goals are descriptive and analytical, not aspirational. Its focus is on the
