Investment Capacity and Employment
\par
Effects
\par
In 1974, there was a widespread belief
\par
in the United States that over the
\par
then coming decade employment con-
\par
straints or investment capacity limits
\par
would prohibit the transition to a
\par
much greater reliance on domestic ener-
\par
gy supplies. Although this specter of
\par
