Definition
\par
"The Conserver Society is one which: promotes economy of design in all systems, i.e.,
\par
'doing more with less'; favours reuse or recycling and, wherever possible, reduction
\par
at source of materials used; questions the stimulation of excessive per-capita demand
\par
for consumer goods by modern marketing techniques; and, recognizes that a diversity
\par
of solutions in many systems such as energy and transportation, might in effect
\par
increase their overall economy, stability and capacity to respond to changing
\par
circums tances. ,,( 9)
\par
Background studies
\par
One useful study on the "Selective Conserver Society" was done by GAMMA. GAMMA, an
\par
interdisciplinary group composed of professors from the universities of Montreal and
\par
McGill, was founded in 1974 to conduct futures research. They investigated a "con-
\par
serving society" and worked out some of the policy options and their implications to
\par
achieve it. The GAMMA study was divided into two phases. The first phase resulted
\par
in the publication (in July 1975) of a think-piece which outlined the theoretical
\par
basis for the task. In the fall of 1976, the second phase was published in a four-
\par
volume report(lO)which developed five scenarios of the future around'the theme
\par
conservation/non-conservation. For example, the CSI scenario is one of rational
\par
conserving society which could be expressed as "doing more with less". The Cs2
\par
scenario depicts a stable state with the theme "doing the same with less". The Cs 3
\par
scenario is the most radical of the three conserver societies and assumes a funda-
\par
mental value change. It would imply an absolute reduction in scale. Its theme is
\par
"doing less with less". The Ministry of State for Science and Technology also
\par
conducted five seminars held across Canada, on "The Conserver Society: The Techno-
\par
logical Challenge". Recently the Department of Energy, Mines and Resources publi-
\par
shed a study on Energy Conservation in Canada (EP 77-7). This report describes
\par
