Now let us elaborate on the tasks of R+D planning and forecasting for the above
\par
classes of R+D programs.
\par
For technologies of class 1, which are now subject to industrial testing and will
\par
be commercialized within the next 4 to G years, the major problems are connected
\par
with the organization of their industrial deployment. As these problems are
\par
solved almost completely at the medium-term planning stage of ESS development,
\par
there are no choices left in the sphere of R+D planning. Thus, the main tasks to
\par
be completed while making the medium-term planning projections for class 1 of R+D
\par
programs are: construction of pilot series of industrial samples of new technolo-
\par
gies and reaching the projected values of their output characteristics; distribu-
\par
tion of responsibilities among building and, partially, projecting firms; mastering
\par
serial production of equipment and distribution of resources in related industrial
