\par
The macro-economic model of Norman-Rogner /1966/ used in the system
\par
of models of IIASA was a successful attempt to build a model which
\par
is sufficiently accurate to cover the basic investment peculiarities,
\par
leaving aside the maximum possible amount of details with a view of
\par
the long-term orientation of the model (1990-2030) and the informa-
\par
tion difficulties arising in connection with the world's regions.It
\par
was decided to build a single-sectoral structural model aryplying an
\par
aonroach based on production and consumer functions in aggregated
\par
form and including a certain number of imDortant macro-economic fac-
\par
tors such as for example aggregated factors of investments and con-
\par
sumntion growth. This apnroach allows coincidence in macro-economic
\par
sense but gives limited possibilities for the output information
\par
needed for the model of energy demand and of ES development. The
\par
nossibilities to assess the energy strategies by means of the model
\par
are also limited.
\par
The now existing economic models in Bulgaria are mainly oriented to-
\par
ward medium-term and long-term planning. The most developed of them-
\par
