Model of Energy Demand.
\par
The model uses information from the economic model and information
\par
about demographic, social and technological development and policy,
\par
and assesses the components of energy demand in the country.
\par
Modeling of energy demand occupies a prominent place in the studies
\par
of ES development. It is determined not only by the fact that the
\par
energy demand, reflecting the ties between society and energy, de-
\par
termines the necessary scale of its development. Modelling of energy
\par
demand and particularly so of long-term demand is extremely com-
\par
plicated from methodical point of view. IIASA stUdies in the oeriod
\par
1965-1966 including those of the author of the present paper,- direc-
\par
ted at the methodical clarification of the problem, can be divided
\par
into two categories: studies oriented at the better clarification of
\par
the mechanism and interties between energy demand and social and te-
\par
chnological development (factor analysis, economic analysis, inter-
\par
national comparisons etc) and studies of forecasting methods based
\par
on these ties, These studies give us ground to believe that an acceo-
\par
tible forecasting of energy demand can be done through a flexible, ..
\par
not fully formalized research procedure of a detailed scenario ana-
\par
lysis of the economic, social and technological aspects of develop-
\par
ment. Such a procedure, initially developed at IEJE\_Grenoble,France
\par
was subsequently adapted in IIASA in two versions: MUSE and t1EDEE\_2.
