\par
The most important data were:
\par
- an average growth of GNP of 3\%,
\par
an average growth of domestic energy demand of 2.9\%,
\par
an average growth of industrial energy demand of 4.4\%,
\par
an average growth of residential energy demand of 1.3\%.
\par
The calculation of an optimal reference scenario for the period 1976-2000 for the
\par
Dutch energy sector showed some interesting results.
\par
a. In spite of a very moderate growth of energy demand the oil imports did increase
\par
sharply, see Fig. I. The refinery capacity stayed at its 1976-level and in 1995
\par
oil refineries will reach a 90\% degree of capacity utilization which is now
\par
about 65\%.
