Demand mode 1 :
\par
The demand model is intended to forecast the average quality of
\par
Japanese people's life (QOL), level of industrial activities and energy
\par
demand required to support the living standard and industrial production
\par
QOL is expressed by a combination of 5 basic needs, namely foods,
\par
clothing, housing, general life and national needs. In the development
\par
of the forecasting procedures, each need was related to the population,
\par
income per capita, saturation factors and etc.
\par
The energy demand in each end use market was estimated using the 5
\par
basic needs. For industrial markets, the amount of end-use products
\par
and materials for industrial production required to meet the respective
\par
estimated needs were forecasted in due consideration of future indus-
\par
trial structure and target levels for imports and exports. The amount
\par
of energy required to produce these products and materials were esti-
\par
mated for each industry and facility. For transportation markets,
\par
demand by type of transportation was related to the amount of passenger
\par
vehicles and ton-kilometers of freight, which were functions of the
\par
basic needs. Residential energy demand was divided into 6 sectors,
\par
that is, space heating, cooling, water heating, cooking, motive power
\par
and lighting/electronics, which were related to the size of houses,
\par
the size of household, saturation of appliances and the basic needs.
