TECHNOLOGY ASSESSMENT
\par
In order to support the development of an R.D\&D strategy it is important to assess
\par
the relative benefits of new technologies.
\par
The scenarios calculated with the MARKALmode1 show implementation levels of new
\par
technologies in different scenarios. This is an important information but certain-
\par
ly not sufficient for technology assessment. The implementation level does not
\par
relate to the specific market of a technology and shows neither the energy input
\par
requirements of the technologies nor the economics and as such does not really
\par
reveal how crucial the technologies are in terms of a relative benefit.
\par
Some attempts were made. however. to shed more light on the expected benefits of
\par
these technologies using analytical methods. The limitations of these approaches
\par
should be kept in mind. Examples of factors that they do not take into account
\par
are:
\par
- relative weighting of scenarios.
\par
- need for R.D\&D.
\par
- cost of R.D\&D (including impact of R.D\&D on technology characteris-
\par
tics).
\par
- technology impact on environment and society.
\par
- special properties of new technologies (e.g. f1uidised bed combustors
\par
can use low grade fuel).
\par
- unit size of technologies (MARKAL uses continuous variables and can
\par
to technologies at only a fraction of their unit
\par
slZe) .
