DISCUSSION
\par
The model described above has been used essentially to answer questions of the
\par
"What if {$\bullet\bullet\bullet$} " type, both for the analysis of past decisions, as well as for future
\par
planning of the energy sector. As a matter of fact, this type of aFproach is
\par
probabaly the most useful one for the decision-making authorities. There are
\par
considerable uncertainties in various aspects of energy planning, and it would be
\par
naive to assume that these uncertainties can be resolved by the use of a model, no
\par
matter how sophisticated the methodology.
\par
Interactions with decision-making authorities also indicate a need to keep the model
\par
as simple as possible. There are several reasons for this, the predominant one
\par
being the ease with which communication can be established between modeller and
\par
decision-maker. Furthermore, the interpretation of results is also simpler to make.
