ABSTRACT
\par
Alternative energy/environment futures for Austria for the period 1977-2015 are
\par
presented. These futures provide a means of examining alternative energy strate-
\par
gies for Austria and of considering some of their environmental implications. Each
\par
future is developed within a framework of policies and assumptions about socio-
\par
economic structure, lifestyle, technology of energy use and supply, and environ-
\par
mental management. A range of policies related to issues such as energy conser-
\par
vation, fuel choices and strategies, and environmental protection are examined by
\par
comparing the scenario results and their sensitivity to varying parameters. The
\par
main tool used in the study is a system of regional energy/environment models
\par
developed at IIASA and the University of Wisconsin. The results of the study in-
\par
clude descriptions of future Austrian Energy consumption by sector and fuel, of
\par
alternative energy supply systems, and of many of the environmental impacts asso-
\par
ciated with the Austrian energy system. The findings show a strong departure in
\par
the downward direction from historical trends in growth of energy use. The study
\par
was conducted in an institutional format which provided frequent interaction with
\par
a large number of individuals and Austrian institutions for whom the results would
\par
be of interest.
\par
