\par
T planning horizon.
\par
It is clear that if it is possible that R=X=Y=O, then it gives an optimal solution
\par
for the criterion (6). In actual, however, it is impossible because we must meet
\par
demands for each products, which is formulated as
\par
yX 2: D,
\par
(7)
\par
where,
\par
