\par
This exercise was done for demonstrative purposes. A considerable amount of
\par
refinement can and should be done to establish better future sensitivities to
\par
input factors.
\par
Over the somewhat longer term one should distinguish for each technology an
\par
"estimation phase", a "learning phase" and a "maturity phase (See Fig. 12). This
\par
will show that the relative advantage of different types of technology and their
\par
combined impact on the average energy price can vary considerably over time. The
\par
method can then be used to determine the main sensitivities, optimal start-up date
\par
and the best production site-market correlation - in a world in which costs,
\par
prices and economic activity levels will increasingly reflect regional (rather
\par
than global) developments.
\par
CONCLUSIONS
\par
It is said that if one were to put all energy price experts in the world head
\par
to foot they would never reach a conclusion.
\par
We leave it to the reader to draw his own inferences from the
\par
thoughts and material presented.
