\par
Uncertainties in factors affecting expenditure (eg cost data) and affecting
\par
capacity commissioned (eg system parameters, policy decisions) introduce
\par
uncertainties in the system expenditure and therefore in the estimate of the cost
\par
benefit of one commissioning programme over another. It is therefore important to
\par
assess the range of confidence which might be ascribed to a given estimate of
\par
system cost benefit. Some estimate can be made of this uncertainty by the repeated
\par
application of the DISCOUNT program using suitably perturbed values in the input
\par
data, but the interpretation of the results is usually difficult and the practical
\par
difficulties of carrying out a sufficiently detailed study are prohibitive. A
\par
computer program, RISKAN, has therefore been developed to estimate with a high
\par
degree of precision, and with a reasonable expenditure of computing time, the
\par
uncertainties in system benefits which would arise due to uncertainties in
\par
constituent items.
