\emph{2. The Acceptable Level of Inaccuracy}
\par
\emph{(a) The Current Conflicting Standards}
\par
Once a statement is subject to the antifraud securitites laws, the inquiry
\par
becomes whether the statement is false or "untrue." 4 7 Development of the implied
\par
representation doctrine broadened the scope of the inquiry. Unfortunately, the
\par
courts' handling of statements concerning prospective information has been
\par
incongruous. Variations in vague terms used by issuers of projections, in an
\par
effort to limit their surety, compound the problem of deciphering the statements'
\par
meaning. The courts tend to mix the nebulous standards of good faith and
\par
reasonable basis in their analyses.
\par
Inconsistencies are seen most clearly in the treatment of the relationship
\par
between the explicit assertion and the degree of support constituting a reasonable
\par
basis for the forecast. Given the inherent uncertainty of prospective information,
