""' Scienter
\par
deals with the requisite degree of culpability of the defendant and is not
\par
specifically concerned with the content of the statement. Determining culpability
\par
is a factual issue that requires the review of the entire disclosure situation.
\par
Moreover, it is influenced by several factors such as the degree of investor
\par
reliance, the purpose for the statement, the relationship of the parties, the
\par
materiality of the information, and the personal interest of the speaker. As a
\par
result, the \emph{Hochfelder }decision was not directed at the misrepresentation element
\par
but rather the standard for culpability, which represents a legal policy decision.
\par
Second, any conflict between scienter and the reasonable basis test is more
\par
apparent than real. A broad application of \emph{Hochfelder }that would require a
\par
