deseasonalized single exponential smoothing outperformed other simple models
\par
such as moving averages and the naive models. While the results from this
\par
competition are only generally applicable to specific forecasting situations, it
\par
does provide information about the tendencies and relative abilities of the various
\par
methods, as well as the factors affecting forecast accuracy. Popular methods
\par
such as moving averages, trend-line analysis, and straight-line projection were
\par
inferior to the exponential smoothing models and several of the more sophisticated
\par
models such as Parzen's and Lewandowski's methods. Also, classical
\par
decomposition, which is rather unfamiliar to many companies, could be used
\par
to improve the accuracy of the simpler methods by deseasonalizing shorter term
\par
data. Based on the competition's results, companies should explore the use of
\par
various methods, especially Holt-Winters', Parzen's, and Lewandowski's.'9
