Along with these general statements, companies should be required to provide
\par
additional information concerning the uncertainty of the forecasts. There are
\par
two basic approaches for determining forecast uncertainty: \textbf{(1) }present validity,
\par
which is an independent assessment of the actual forecast; and (2) prior validity,
\par
which expresses uncertainty based on the measurement of past performance.
\par
Generally, prior validity is well suited to sophisticated statistical analysis, but
\par
less adaptable to judgmental forecast methods.
