\par
The empirical evidence conflicts regarding the value of qualified audit reports
\par
based on stock market reaction. Methodological problems in the studies prevent
\par
drawing clear, absolute conclusions on the incremental information content of
\par
these reports. Indeed, it may be virtually impossible to isolate empirically the
\par
impact of qualified audit reports per se on stock prices given the different levels
\par
of seriousness of various types of qualifications and the presence of other
\par
information necessarily attached to a qualified report. Therefore, this research
\par
must be viewed with these limitations in mind. Criticism that this research is
\par
