\par
often are restricted to a limited number of
\par
intervention types. This population may be de-
\par
fined by policies transmitted from a unit to
\par
which this unit is accountable, or it may be
\par
defined by the policies of the unit itself.
\par
Examoles: mental hospitals; clinics; private
\par
practitioners who define their own population
\par
admission-discharge policies.
\par
4. Case workers: these are units of the MHDS that
\par
have responsibility for individual clients but
\par
who make no policy decisions on populations.
\par
