The future of reform appears bleak. The present system produces inade-
\par
quate internalization of the costs of occupational illnesses, yet many of the
\par
proposed reforms would be even less effective. Elimination of restrictive stan-
\par
dards and the creation of a causal presumption would be desirable improve-
\par
