The takeover statute and rules now embody a compromise. A potential bidder
\par
need not disclose its own ownership interest or plans to seek control of a target
\par
until it owns more than five percent of a class of stock. But the bidder may not
\par
tip institutions or other separate persons about an impending offer after it has
\par
taken substantial steps to commence a tender offer. The prohibition on tipping
\par
institutions (warehousing) or individuals will operate before a five percent own-
\par
ership interest is achieved, as long as a substantial step is taken toward the com-
\par
mencement of a tender offer. Rule 14e-3 does not define what a "substantial step
\par
