\par
tion. It is true that determined detective work occasionally succeeds in
\par
demonstrating the falsity of such stories. It equally is true that current law will
\par
encourage the Holmesian "bad men" 263 of the securities world to fabricate ex-
\par
cuses and reduce the number of cases that the SEC or the Department of Justice
\par
successfully can prosecute.
\par
Another type of "innocent" is more likely to inspire sympathy. An inventor
\par
might buy stock in a specific firm before agreeing to sell or license a new product
\par
to that same firm. Alternatively the inventor might short-sell rival firms' stock
\par
before negotiating a sales or licensing-agreement. 26 4 If the stock purchases or
\par
short-sales are made before negotiations commence with a specific firm, no plain-
\par
