\par
Whether or not to rescale the judgments is a delicate matter, one that
\par
depends upon the researcher's degree of confidence in the theoretical
\par
model that is being tested and his confidence in the validity of the scale
\par
on which the judgments are measured. For example, Lampel and Ander-
\par
son (1968) found a significant interaction between visual and verbal
\par
information in an impression formation task. This interaction could have
\par
