Descriptive studies of probability assessment can be helpful for both assess-
\par
ment and evaluation purposes. Psychological studies have provided useful infor-
\par
mation concerning the use of different response modes, possible response biases,
\par
the ability of individuals to express their uncertainty in terms of probabilities, and
\par
